    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d940">

                <pb facs="0905" n="893" xml:id="pg893"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.515/29: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Moose</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-25T20:00:00+03:06">August 25, 1943—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 26—7:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>99. Department’s 52, August 17, midnight.<anchor n="90" xml:id="d940-f1"/> I see
                    no way in which suggested procedure could be improved upon. It is requested that
                    this Legation be supplied with copies of any requests, reports or
                    recommendations relative to silver for Saudi Arabia not submitted from here.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moose</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d940-f1" n="90" xml:id="d940-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 1172 to the Minister in Egypt, <ref target="#pg891">p.
